{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the reviewed tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. I did not request any implementation source. The clauses below are mapped to tests.\n\n**Combine and include every applicable contribution.**\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` checks that the subject's declaration and the declarations it cites are supplied.\n- The same test checks the terms it uses, the owning test item, and the exact text of an example subject.\n- It also checks that distant requirements and old evidence inputs are excluded.\n- `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` checks which reference edges contribute inputs.\n- `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` compares the exact full input list for file anchors.\n- `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` checks node-level anchors.\n- `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` and `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` cover reference-owning nodes and discovery exclusions.\n- `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]` and `fn[earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward]` cover the rule that earlier evidence is not carried forward.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs` has tests for the citation and book-commentary review kinds, and for site reviews: `fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]`, `fn[book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance]` and `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]`. These check the mandatory sets for those subject kinds.\n\n**Deduplicate identical selections.**\n- `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` cites the same requirement twice and shares a term across two requirements. It also repeats a built-in `habeas:util` citation. It asserts each of these appears exactly once and that the total is 5.\n- The site review test asserts an exact input count of 4.\n- The CLI test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` checks deduplication in evidence.\n\n**Report unresolvable inputs before inference.**\n- `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` checks that preparation fails with `PermissionDenied` and names the path.\n- `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` checks missing files, missing nodes, and ignored anchors.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort]` checks an anchor outside the project.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request]` runs the real CLI. It checks a nonzero exit, that stderr names the path, that the model endpoint is never contacted, and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n\n**Complete set in the initial model request.**\n- The CLI test checks that the initial prompt contains the requirement, the definition, and the test item. It also checks that the implementation text is absent.\n- The citation test checks that the prompt contains the hash of the mandatory item and the declaration text.\n- The site test asserts that `initial.subject` equals the template filled with all mandatory inputs.\n- The `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` test checks the prompt content.\n\n**Local-provider visibility.**\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` checks that untracked files are available.\n- `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` checks ignored directories and a symlink alias.\n- `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` and the other denial tests check ignored and outside-project files.\n\n**Out of scope.**\n- The duty on contributing requirements to cite this requirement and define their contributions is carried by those requirements.\n- The abort details under `read_denial.mandatory` are a cited requirement, so I did not reassess them.\n\nI found no plausible violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "24022a85373a405b0fb3408b99edf1d1bbc96fd33788256d087c885bb430c4d7",
